From 8d817b62d0a15faa62aa8d7da2325f742d3e6ad1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 17:38:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Official collector: publish credit statistics only when
 captured 22:30-23:59 Taipei; carry the last night capture unchanged

GPT's 2026-11-06 morning report: the morning bundle carried credit statistics
captured at 05:26/09:50 Taipei, which conflicts with the Site rule
"no credit re-capture before 22:30 Taipei; keep the original observation date
and check time".

- run_official_collector.sh auto mode collects credit statistics only from
  22:30 to 23:59 Taipei (same rule as the Site's taiwanCreditCaptureAllowed).
- publish_official_import.py refuses a statistics.json captured outside that
  window (reported in errors), whatever the mode.
- When a run has no new night capture, the previous bundle's statistics.json
  is carried byte for byte (same SHA, original capturedAt) if it is a night
  capture no older than 30 hours; the manifest lists it under "carried" or
  explains why not in "carryNote".
- Third night schedule at 23:35 Taipei because GitHub often delays or skips.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PERuCJaQBxpqs7Rn24Bma8
